.TH REMOVE 2
.SH NAME
remove \- remove a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B import "vsys:libuser"
.PP
.nf
.B "remove :: proc(path: string) -> i64"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Remove
resolves
.I path
in the caller's name space and removes it from the directory that
contains it.
If
.I path
is a directory, the server that holds it may refuse unless the directory
is empty.
.PP
The channel to the file is spent whether or not the server agreed to
remove it: a failed
.I remove
still consumes the walk that found the file, exactly as a failed 9P
.B Tremove
does.
.SH SOURCE
.B sys/libuser/sys.odin
.br
.B kernel/user/syscall.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR intro (2),
.IR open (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Answers zero on success and a negative
.B \-errno
on failure; see
.IR errstr (2).
.SH BUGS
There is no rename; a program that wants one copies the file under the
new name and removes the old one.
